A||N||11||FieroJoe||Stereo Sound much better while leaning back?||||5||
Z||000000||FieroJoe||05-30-2001||10:41 PM||||Today I noticed a very interesting thing about my stereo.  As I was driving along, I leaned back all the way into the seat and rested my head on the headrest (I dont normally drive all lain back like this, I dont think anyone does for that matter...)  What a difference in sound!!!  I never realized until just then that all I have been hearing from my stereo is the front 4x10's and just my sub (stock system).  I mean I can understand the headrest blocking some of the sound from the driver's side 4x6, but even the pass side too!  I played around with moving the seat a bit and it sounded so much better.<P>The bad thing is though, I can't move my driver's seat enough to make it sound so much more fuller and still be able to drive comfortably.<P>Is there anything that I can do about this?  I was wondering what headrest speaker seats would sound like.  I've never been in a Fiero with those.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||05-30-2001||10:48 PM||||You can adjust the fade control or get an aftermarket system with a digital surround sound. With my processor I can vary the delay and have many different set-up's.<BR>It makes the car sound larger and so much better.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierodave2001||05-30-2001||11:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroJoe:<BR><B>I was wondering what headrest speaker seats would sound like</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The 85SE I had, came with the Speakers in the headrest.<P>From what I remember, the sound was pretty good. Maybe find someone with the same,<BR>and listen to it.<P>You may want to find some seats of that year & swap out||||reg||6
Z||000003||Philphine||05-30-2001||11:12 PM||||could be that you were getting away from your drivers side front speaker and letting the passenger side front add a little more to what you're hearing. it's the equal pathlenth thing you hear hard core stereo guys talk about. it's the reason why people put speakers in the dead pedal/kick panel area. if you got your "gangstah lean on" it might sound better still.||||reg||1
Z||000004||SPDFREK||05-30-2001||11:22 PM||||I have a VR3 "Virtual Surround Retrieval Prossor" in all my cars, I noticed the same lack of sound in my nova and bought one, Now i put them in all my cars, and all the cars that I build systems for. The sound is awsome! the specs on these are:<P>Total Harmonic distortion........0.1%<BR>By Pass Gain.............-3DB<BR>Feed through Gain...........(in VR3 Mode) -13.3DB<BR>amp specs are:<P>Frequency Respon......20-20000 Hz<BR>RCA level Input.........100Mv<BR>speaker line input.......1.6V<BR>power requirments......11-16V DC<BR>total Power out.......*200 Watts PMPO<BR>RMS..........80 Watts (20x4)<P>Hope this helps.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>'88 Fiero 4cycl Turbo,<BR>'88 Fiero GT,<BR>'72 Nova 383 stroker||||reg||1
Z||000005||FLASHY||05-30-2001||11:24 PM||||I've listened to one with speakers in the seats and they sounded really good. It added a more surround sound and the clarity was nicer too.||||reg||14
Z||000006||FieroJoe||05-31-2001||07:35 AM||||How much can I expect to pay for a decent sound processor?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Oreif||05-31-2001||09:23 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroJoe:<BR><B>How much can I expect to pay for a decent sound processor?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>The one I have is an Audio Control ESP-2.<BR>It's on sale for $135.oo at:<BR> <A HREF="http://audio-n-more.com/audio_control.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://audio-n-more.com/audio_control.htm</A> <P>This unit is perfect for the Fiero, Small size and easy to install. It has a seperate control that I mounted under the dash between the dash pod and radio pod.<P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroJoe||05-31-2001||09:40 AM||||Oreif - I have seen the pics of your amp install on the rear passenger firewall, I assume you mounted the main unit there with everything else.  Do you have a pic of the little control unit that you are talking about?<P>I will say that the price for that processor is not as much as I thought it would be.  Right now I'm saving my money towards a sunroof swap (anyone got a complete kit cheap?), but I will definatly keep that in mind.  You'll definatly be hearing from me if I ever install one  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000009||Oreif||05-31-2001||10:26 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroJoe:<BR><B>Oreif - I have seen the pics of your amp install on the rear passenger firewall, I assume you mounted the main unit there with everything else.  Do you have a pic of the little control unit that you are talking about?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Here is a pic of the unit and the controller for it. I'll try and get pics of it installed in my car soon. (I have the white case) The phone type of cable for the controller is about 10 feet long. The short one in the pic is just an example.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Esp2.jpg">  <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 05-31-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||Alex4mula||05-31-2001||11:39 AM||||Orief; Would that work with a 3-pre-amp out? I have front, rear & sub. Searched Audio Control web but couldn't find any info on it.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Oreif||05-31-2001||12:05 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Alex4mula:<BR><B>Orief; Would that work with a 3-pre-amp out? I have front, rear & sub. Searched Audio Control web but couldn't find any info on it.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The unit has 1 pair in and 2 pairs out. The 2 pairs out are not the same. One is a "thru" output. The thru output has no delay/effects out of it. I just went from the head unit (1 pair of RCA's) into the  ESP-2, then 1 pair out to the crossover (which splits the high's and the sub) then into the amps.<P>The reason you can't find info on Audio Controls website is because they don't make this unit anymore. (Also that is why they hard to find for sale) They also don't make the ESP-3 (adds center channel outputs)<BR>They are working on a new processor. For those wanting to get this unit, I'd get them before they are all gone.<BR>||||reg||1
